From: vbardales <virginie.bardales@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:33:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] test(language): exercise the window this fix exists for

The fix could not be unit tested - both halves need RimWorld - and CONTRIBUTING
says as much: anything touching the game is proved by running the suite. So it
gets what it should have had from the start, a scenario.

Switching language is the one thing that empties activeLanguage, so
language-steps.feature walks through it and back. The proof is structural
rather than an assertion: on the broken code the snapshot published during that
window throws out of the runner, the run ends with exitReason
"infrastructure-error", and the file never reaches its second scenario.

The step comes with it, because no vanilla one could switch language and suites
were each writing their own - one of them asserted straight after the call and
read the old language on a slow machine. SelectLanguage does not finish inside
the call, so the step waits for activeLanguage and declares TimeoutSeconds,
above the five seconds a step gets by default.

AI-assisted: Claude Code

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
